senses.gloss:
Dṛḍhadhanu,
(1) (cf. prec.) n. of a cakravartin, previous incarnation of Śākyamuni: Mv 〔i.60.14〕 (˚nunā, instr.); n. of an ancient king, perhaps the same: Mv 〔ii.146.19〕 (˚nuḥ, n. sg.);
(2) n. of a yakṣa: Māy 〔56〕.

Dṛḍhabāhu,
(1) n. of a Buddha in the nadir: Mv 〔i.124.8〕;
(2) n. of a disciple of Śākyamuni: Mv 〔i.182.17〕.

Dṛḍhamati,
(1) m., n. of a man (in Śūraṃgamasamādhisūtra): Śikṣ 〔91.8 ff.〕;
(2) f., n. of a girl attendant on Subhadrā (1): Gv 〔52.2〕.

Dṛḍhavīrya,
(1) n. of a former Buddha: Mv 〔i.139.8〕;
(2) n. of a kiṃnara king: Kv 〔3.4〕.
